"mdjnl96zs16v2ec4wbbzg85c", "ape-reflect-prompt-trim-first", "must_not", "ape", "ape.reflect truncation ROOT CAUSE confirmed (precise, for the next sprint): the prompt is ~7685 tokens median (max 7719), NOT the ~5800 in CLAUDE.md. Per-slot KV = 32768 ctx / 4 parallel = 8192. That leaves only ~507 tokens for output. 191/200 recent invalid responses cluster at 490-520 tokens_out — hitting the ~507 ceiling and truncating mid-JSON. The 9 valid responses had shorter prompts (down to 5719 tok), leaving room (744 median tokens_out). ape.reflect max_tokens floors at 2000 (llm_reflector.go:127-130) but that is never reached — the KV slot caps first. Fix options: (1) reduce --parallel 4->2 (slot 16384); (2) raise --ctx-size; (3) TRIM the ape.reflect prompt (~7685 tok is the real problem, highest leverage, also speeds inference); (4) chunk reflection. Prompt-trim is likely best: fixes truncation AND latency. Next sprint after PR #461 merges."
"sqe0bca027ynqkx10cd9j90q", "audit-before-prune", "must_not", "DATAPRUNE-AUDIT-001 audit complete (non-destructive)", "DATAPRUNE-AUDIT-001 audit complete (non-destructive). Non-conforming TSDB/file data enumerated: PRUNE TARGETS = (A) 2111 invalid-JSON rows in object/array tasks [ape.reflect 1890 concentrated 06-11..06-13 truncation window, rerank_cross 184, evaluate_llm 18, query_classify 18, classify 1], (B) 21135 error/empty rows [mdemg data clean target], (C) rerank mislabeled archive 6894 events/202 files/21M + valid_golden 108 leaked rows + ~14 stale April baselines. Total ~23246 TSDB rows (~22.7% of 102392). NOT prune targets (schema/reward mismatch, data is fine): hidden.summarize 72 (prose vs object schema), string-schema tasks the jsonb check false-flags (intent_translate 4260/codegen 823/synthesize 486 emit valid bare strings), jiminy.evaluate. KEY AUDIT PITFALL: never run a jsonb-validity prune predicate against string-schema tasks. The 87%-of-54k fear was wrong: ape.reflect corruption is only 1890 rows in the recent truncation window, post-fix rows valid. Prune execution is operator-gated per category, backup-first/small-batch."
"aegqqbtidh44w3qja6763xyt", "auto-00f5f84ea9a3", "should", "Neo4j space hygiene: deleted 24 junk/test/demo spaces (~143k nodes, export-backed-up) for live-testing clean slate — l", "Neo4j space hygiene: deleted 24 junk/test/demo spaces (~143k nodes, export-backed-up) for live-testing clean slate — lnl-demo-whk 51483, whk-wms 49470, linear 10032 (dormant), e2e-test 10918, ubts-load 6019, + template-artifact spaces ({{SPACE_ID}}, ${test_space}, uats-batch-{{$timestamp}}) + assorted test. Retained mdemg-dev, demo, mdemg, mdemg-codebase, global. Fixed 2 real bugs: (1) mdemg space delete pre-check counted only MemoryNode but deletes all labels → SymbolNode-only spaces (e2e-test 10918 SymbolNodes) silently survived with no-nodes; now counts all labels. (2) mdemg space list panicked sid.(string) on nil space_id; query now excludes null/empty space_id + nil-guarded. Blank/null space_id = global infra (schema/signal/interview/scraper, queried w/o space_id BY DESIGN, kept null per operator) + 155 empty J17/J12 test MemoryNodes (junk, staged for delete). Follow-up: UATS/UBTS runners create unsubstituted-template spaces ({{SPACE_ID}}) — should reject placeholder space_ids."
"po8w22fqiv42b7vknvh42eoe", "auto-01288edd49b1", "must", "REQUIREMENT (formalized 2026-05-01 by reh3376): Live system testing is a required testing tier for every sprint that tou", "REQUIREMENT (formalized 2026-05-01 by reh3376): Live system testing is a required testing tier for every sprint that touches code paths exercised in production. Mocked unit + integration tests are necessary but not sufficient. Tier 3 E2E means: the real binary running against the real services it depends on, with real outputs observed via TSDB queries / Grafana panels / log inspection — not mocked clients. Evidence basis: across Phase 11.6.x, 11.6.2, and 12.0-12.6, every major defect was caught in live smoke runs while unit/integration tests passed. Six cutover-bypass sites, five latent UVTS-runner defects, the host.docker.internal DNS issue, the panel-3 SQL false-positive — all surfaced only when running the live system. Sprint plans must include a verification-checklist item of the form: live smoke: run X against the real system, observe Y in TSDB/Grafana/logs, confirm Z. Surprise bugs caught during live smoke get their own follow-up fix-commit; do not silently roll them into the sprint commit. The live system can be the operator local stack (mdemg native binary + Docker Compose) — the point is real I/O on the real wire, not production scale."
