"pbcmknqz7rjbgjlvctgb3d72", "auto-a77a769e417a", "must_not", "At 105+ phases, 2000+ line API docs, and 60+ files per commit, the planning protocol is not overhead — it is the only", "At 105+ phases, 2000+ line API docs, and 60+ files per commit, the planning protocol is not overhead — it is the only thing preventing drift. Skipping context research leads to false negatives (e.g., claiming Jiminy healthz/ready endpoints do not exist when /readyz already had Jiminy health logic at line 164 of handlers.go). The more complex the codebase gets, the more plan-first discipline pays for itself. NEVER skip the research step before declaring something does not exist."
