"wyl4j8zswjxtmqxryzw59777", "iterate-break-fix-verify", "must", "CRITICAL PROCESS: When fixing a pipeline, a fix is NOT done when the code compiles or tests pass", "CRITICAL PROCESS: When fixing a pipeline, a fix is NOT done when the code compiles or tests pass. It is done when the actual end-to-end observable output (dashboard metric, API response, log line) shows the correct value. Each fix must be followed by running the pipeline and verifying the output. If the output is still wrong, trace why and fix the next break. This is iterative — do not declare victory until the metric reads correctly. The J17 protocol fix required 12 breaks across 5 iterations of run-trace-fix cycles, not just the initial 7 identified statically."
"gwc3twp6cpe1tdrfs7zcet5w", "jiminy-uuid-cuid2-enforce", "should", "Decision: CUIDv2 enforcement is now documented as a Jiminy-enforceable constraint", "Decision: CUIDv2 enforcement is now documented as a Jiminy-enforceable constraint. When Jiminy sees uuid.New(), uuid.NewString(), or UUID v4 patterns in identifier generation, it should surface the CUIDv2 requirement. This is the first case study of Jiminy constraint-pipeline failure leading to codebase divergence."
