"ykqvbobzs7bz5zzq8q1tcocr", "live-validation-against-guardrails", "must", "REWARD-CORRECTNESS-001 live Tier 3 finding: scoring real production llm_interactions at the 0", "REWARD-CORRECTNESS-001 live Tier 3 finding: scoring real production llm_interactions at the 0.8 distill gate proved Epic 1 length-neutral rewards recovered 69/72 hidden.summarize rows, but exposed three larger correctness issues NOT fixed by length-neutrality: (1) ape.reflect (54k rows, largest target) json_valid mean 0.133 — ~87% of recent responses are TRUNCATED mid-JSON (prompt ~5800 tok + ~3000 output > 8192 per-slot KV bound = 32768/4); production serving defect, gate correctly rejects them. (2) jiminy.evaluate explanation_quality=0.0 on correct responses — wrong reward for schema {violations,warnings} which has no top-level explanation key. (3) jiminy.synthesize follow_rate/specificity keyword-bag just below 0.8 (deferred). The dominant FT-corpus-correctness problems are truncation + reward/schema mismatch, not length bias. Prune phase must treat truncated invalid-JSON rows as non-conforming."
"yeacdnr9e0ql91drmqckd127", "mandatory-e2e-docs-before-commit", "must", "MANDATORY WORKFLOW: ALWAYS run e2e testing once a new section of development is complete", "MANDATORY WORKFLOW: ALWAYS run e2e testing once a new section of development is complete. ALWAYS update all relevant documentation (specs, phase docs, AGENT_HANDOFF.md, MEMORY.md) BEFORE staging and committing changes. Sequence: implement → e2e test → update docs → stage → commit. No exceptions."
"lq3omb4tx7wm4yraxnmpor8e", "mandatory-feature-docs", "must", "MANDATORY PROCESS: After a new feature is created in the development plan, a documentation file MUST be created that exp", "MANDATORY PROCESS: After a new feature is created in the development plan, a documentation file MUST be created that explains the new functionality and provides links to relevant documentation. IF new APIs or UATS specs are involved, docs/development/API_REFERENCE.md MUST also be updated. This applies to ALL future phases."
