"bj4w17ne1elu2yrh2kida62m", "memory-preservation-backup-integrity", "should", "SKILL: CMS Self-Improvement — Core Directive + Memory Protection", "CMS Memory Protection Constraint: (1) Trigger Neo4j backup of mdemg-dev space when no active codebase operations are in progress. (2) Check CMS health via /healthz during sessions; investigate anomalies immediately. (3) Record critical observations (corrections, key decisions) with high surprise scores to ensure persistence. (4) On DB failure, check backups/ directory, restore Neo4j, verify mdemg-dev space integrity."
"uctrlnyxd9af96szaz671g92", "must-comment-sprint-summary-on-pr", "must", "RULE: ALWAYS add a detailed sprint summary as a PR comment every time a new PR is created, including auto-created PRs fr", "RULE: ALWAYS add a detailed sprint summary as a PR comment every time a new PR is created, including auto-created PRs from pushing to a dev branch. Auto-created PRs have no body by default, so the comment is the only structured record. Summary must cover: sprint ID/title, epics completed, commits per epic (with short hashes), findings/issues addressed, key metrics (test results, empirical data), live integration test results, and verification gates (build/lint/test). Detect the PR via gh pr list --state open after push, then gh pr comment <num> --body-file -. This is proactive — part of done for every PR."
"g4tzgs1ffjkykh4v0sf3q553", "must-e2e-live-data-verify", "must", "Every sprint that touches a pipeline must include an end-to-end verification step against live data, not just go test", "Every sprint that touches a pipeline must include an end-to-end verification step against live data, not just go test ./.... Unit tests alone are insufficient — must verify actual observable output from the running system."
"xkvytpf7e4m3xjy5aj40m9q4", "must-enforce-jiminy-constraints", "must", "ARCHITECTURAL DIRECTIVE 2026-08-01 (operator): Jimini's purpose is to ENFORCE hard constraints on the main LLM's behavio", "ARCHITECTURAL DIRECTIVE 2026-08-01 (operator): Jimini's purpose is to ENFORCE hard constraints on the main LLM's behavior, not merely advise. When the main LLM violates a Jiminy constraint, the user MUST be alerted. Jiminy's overarching purpose is to force the stateless + probabilistic nature of an LLM into a stateful + deterministic set of behaviors. The enforcement cycle MUST be RSIC-governed so Jiminy continuously learns from its own enforcement decisions (false-blocks weaken the constraint; missed-violations strengthen or extend coverage). The current default-advisory + opt-in /strict architecture is MISALIGNED with this intent — /strict should be the DEFAULT, coverage MUST extend beyond Write/Edit to include Bash (and any other action-producing tool), and violations MUST both block AND alert. This directive supersedes any prior framing of Jiminy as advisory-by-design."
"xgun8uz3hlvnujoq9amb0zf6", "must-enforce-jiminy-constraints", "should", "ARCHITECTURAL DIRECTIVE 2026-08-01 (operator): Jimini's purpose is to ENFORCE hard constraints on the main LLM's behavio", "ARCHITECTURAL DIRECTIVE 2026-08-01 (operator): Jimini's purpose is to ENFORCE hard constraints on the main LLM's behavior, not merely advise. When the main LLM violates a Jiminy constraint, the user MUST be alerted. Jiminy's overarching purpose is to force the stateless + probabilistic nature of an LLM into a stateful + deterministic set of behaviors. The enforcement cycle MUST be RSIC-governed so Jiminy continuously learns from its own enforcement decisions (false-blocks weaken the constraint; missed-violations strengthen or extend coverage). The current default-advisory + opt-in /strict architecture is MISALIGNED with this intent — /strict should be the DEFAULT, coverage MUST extend beyond Write/Edit to include Bash (and any other action-producing tool), and violations MUST both block AND alert. This directive supersedes any prior framing of Jiminy as advisory-by-design."
"necnzrfavaag8uzexngv59xs", "must-follow-12-section-format", "must_not", "All sprint development plans MUST follow the standardized 12-section format (v1", "All sprint development plans MUST follow the standardized 12-section format (v1.0). Required sections: Header & Metadata, Problem Statement, Scope & Constraints, Dependencies & Pre-Conditions, Implementation Plan (sequential epics with gates), Testing Plan (3 tiers: unit + integration + e2e — never skip), Commit Strategy, Verification Checklist, Documentation Update (final epic — never cut for time), Risks & Mitigations, Documents Accessed. Optional: Rollback Procedures (for destructive ops). Recall format via: POST /v1/skills/sprint-planning/recall or filter_tags skill:sprint-planning"
