"jp1kcjqzo2g8uee2llcl2zxm", "must-master-data-pipelines", "must", "We cannot make good decisions and properly optimize the effectiveness of the MDEMG framework if we do not have reliable", "We cannot make good decisions and properly optimize the effectiveness of the MDEMG framework if we do not have reliable and consistent data to base our decisions on and drive our algorithms. The correctness and consistency of this data capture is the absolute core base infrastructure — without it the goals and vision of MDEMG can never be achieved. We MUST master these data pipelines and their historical collection."
"ye63j72ni1j8hen8rxhz1bda", "must-pin-mlx-8101", "must", "Local Qwen3", "Local Qwen3.6-35B-A3B MLX teacher endpoint is pinned to http://127.0.0.1:8101/v1. Single-instance enforcement required: distill_driver.py calls enforce_single_mlx_instance() pre-run; any stray mlx_lm.server process aborts with the PID list. Do NOT use :8100 (Docker backend reserves it via IPv6). Canonical port is :8101 on 127.0.0.1. Sprint FT-LORA-DATA §1 Header pins this."
"inpos5znn984sbdkcglp1t63", "must-use-cuid2", "must", "[must] All unique identifiers in MDEMG must use CUIDv2 (nrednav/cuid2), NOT UUID v4", "[must] All unique identifiers in MDEMG must use CUIDv2 (nrednav/cuid2), NOT UUID v4. This is a project-scoped requirement across main repo and all submodules. CUIDv2 is collision-resistant, k-sortable, and shorter. uuid.New() and uuid.NewString() are banned patterns. Use cuid2.Generate() instead."
"ry5tes3xrw90llxdp4nye820", "must-use-cuidv2-by-default", "must_not", "CORRECTION: the previous approach was wrong — never use the unordered LIMIT sample for novelty; this must be replaced", "CORRECTION: the previous approach was wrong — never use the unordered LIMIT sample for novelty; this must be replaced. The earlier assumption was incorrect."
"mw1w51y634tngeumdpx26c5o", "must-use-uxts-frameworks-consistently", "must", "When creating a JSON schema, contract, or test spec that will be used repeatedly, you MUST use the established UxTS fram", "When creating a JSON schema, contract, or test spec that will be used repeatedly, you MUST use the established UxTS framework family rather than ad-hoc JSON: UATS for HTTP API contract tests (docs/api/api-spec/uats/specs/), UITS for UI/cross-component flow specs (docs/tests/uits/specs/), UOBS for observability/metrics, ULTS for LLM prompt contracts, etc. Adding/changing an API response field (e.g. status on /v1/backup/list) MUST update the corresponding UATS spec; UI tab assertions belong in the UITS framework + Playwright, not ad-hoc. The 15 UxTS frameworks are catalogued in docs/tests/UXTS_FRAMEWORK_MATRIX.md and CI-gated via the drift checker."
"y8icw1s1gk7ochvyplxu7g8y", "never-direct-alter-schema", "must_not", "CONSTRAINT: Never modify production database schemas without a migration file", "CONSTRAINT: Never modify production database schemas without a migration file. Always use CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS and index creation with IF NOT EXISTS guards. Direct ALTER TABLE on production is forbidden."
"okosuztxmnxil0x6ywq4eh5m", "never-haiku-for-planning", "must_not", "USER PREFERENCE: When planning complex features or fixes, ALWAYS use the most advanced coding model available (Opus)", "USER PREFERENCE: When planning complex features or fixes, ALWAYS use the most advanced coding model available (Opus). Never delegate planning or architecture to Haiku. Haiku is only for simple mechanical tasks: file searches, grep, status checks. Sub-agent model selection: Haiku=simple/fast, Sonnet=medium analysis, Opus=planning/architecture/complex fixes."
"mihy2vx509twdy0dqlddxmbr", "never-hardcode-config", "should", "CORRECTION: Never hardcode values in production code", "CORRECTION: Never hardcode values in production code. Always use configurable variables (CLI flags, env vars, config files). Hardcoded values create static code that requires source modification to change behavior — users should be able to configure runtime behavior without understanding or modifying the code. Use defaults as fallbacks, but expose every configurable value through the configuration hierarchy. Why: Hardcoded paths, endpoints, space IDs, timeouts, and model names make code non-portable, non-reusable, and require code changes for what should be operational configuration. This was caught in the benchmark runner which had hardcoded CODEBASE_PATH, MDEMG_ENDPOINT, MDEMG_SPACE_ID, etc."
"a5ax6i2owzuwlry7emx0pqkh", "never-skip-discovered-issues", "should", "MANDATORY RULE: Never leave discovered issues unresolved", "MANDATORY RULE: Never leave discovered issues unresolved. When issues are found during development — even if unrelated to the current task — they must be either (1) fixed immediately, or (2) documented and tracked for resolution once the current task set completes. Suggesting to skip, ignore, or defer issues indefinitely is NEVER acceptable. At minimum, note the issue explicitly and return to it. This applies to test failures, bugs, lint warnings, stale data, broken endpoints, missing checks — everything. Jiminy should monitor for and correct any agent behavior that suggests skipping discovered issues."
"iq9wylbhu16eecug2tqtvqm4", "never-start-mdemg-dbs", "must_not", "CRITICAL LESSON: NEVER use mdemg db start when the original Neo4j was launched via docker compose", "CRITICAL LESSON: NEVER use mdemg db start when the original Neo4j was launched via docker compose. docker compose uses volume mdemg_neo4j_data (underscores, project-prefixed) while mdemg db start creates mdemg-neo4j-data (hyphens). The original volume contains ALL CMS memory (34,416 nodes). Always use docker compose up -d neo4j to preserve data. The .env must use NEO4J_PASS=testpassword to match docker-compose.yml."
"w17xt3ozfs1baqghrpnqaic0", "never-trust-unordered-samples", "must", "CORRECTION REINFORCEMENT: never trust an unordered sample for novelty — the earlier assumption was wrong and must not", "CORRECTION REINFORCEMENT: never trust an unordered sample for novelty — the earlier assumption was wrong and must not recur. Use exact nearest-neighbor ranking."
"myya3xf8kpk3wpbo0qonah99", "no-direct-main-commits", "must", "CONSTRAINT: NEVER commit directly to main branch", "CONSTRAINT: NEVER commit directly to main branch. All development work happens on mdemg-dev01. Main is branch-protected — changes reach it only via PR. The auto-pr.yml workflow creates PRs automatically on push to mdemg-dev01. Always verify branch before any git operation: git branch --show-current must show mdemg-dev01."
"tmnsm35onyon3uq7hxmny1m7", "no-stash-for-release", "must_not", "CORRECTION: Never use git stash as a workaround for goreleaser dirty-state checks", "CORRECTION: Never use git stash as a workaround for goreleaser dirty-state checks. The correct approach is to commit all pending changes BEFORE running goreleaser release. If files are not ready to commit, they should be properly handled (committed as WIP, or the release should wait). Stashing to bypass tool checks is a bad practice that leaves orphaned state."
"ya3zhpo6v1ky8v3xjwqcf273", "openai-max-completion-tokens", "must", "RECURRING BUG (3rd occurrence): OpenAI chat/completions API — newer models (gpt-5", "RECURRING BUG (3rd occurrence): OpenAI chat/completions API — newer models (gpt-5.x, gpt-4.1+) REQUIRE the `max_completion_tokens` parameter; `max_tokens` is rejected with HTTP 400 `Unsupported parameter` error. ALL new LLM-calling code that targets OpenAI must use `max_completion_tokens`. MLX-local and legacy OpenAI-compatible endpoints still accept `max_tokens`. Pattern: `token_key = \"max_completion_tokens\" if \"api.openai.com\" in base_url else \"max_tokens\"`. Discovered again 2026-04-22 in `neural/training/distill_driver.py` — patched in _chat_completion(). Check codebase proactively when writing any new OpenAI HTTP wrapper."
"if6icfdlwvvxac68bvddsplh", "own-test-failures-immediately", "must_not", "Standing directive: If a test failure is found during any work, it is my responsibility to fix it immediately", "Standing directive: If a test failure is found during any work, it is my responsibility to fix it immediately. Never leave a failure for someone else. Own every failure you encounter."
"i9e6xjl542a6qxjmbd2tz6c0", "pinned-e2e-test-permanent", "should", "E2E pinned test observation - should be permanent", "E2E pinned test observation - should be permanent"
"johzbd6pbcyvpejc2omshmlt", "plan-mode-before-change", "should", "CRITICAL CORRECTION: Do NOT modify code without first switching to planning mode and creating a development plan", "CRITICAL CORRECTION: Do NOT modify code without first switching to planning mode and creating a development plan. This codebase is too complex for on-the-fly changes without context research. The goreleaser nfpm fix (removing type:glob, adding submodules:recursive) was made as a reactive hotfix without planning — exactly the behavior being constrained. Must enter plan mode BEFORE any code modification, research context, then propose changes. Jiminy should detect and redirect when code modifications are attempted without an active plan."
"udzpmtsiw04sptyodrv7mot2", "prune-guardrail-compliance-check", "must", "DATAPRUNE-AUDIT-001 Category A prune EXECUTED: deleted 1898 genuinely-corrupt invalid-JSON rows from llm_interactions (a", "DATAPRUNE-AUDIT-001 Category A prune EXECUTED: deleted 1898 genuinely-corrupt invalid-JSON rows from llm_interactions (ape.reflect 1879, jiminy.evaluate_llm 18, consulting.classify 1), backup-first to .mdemg-backup-20260613_195431/dataprune/ (38M CSV, all 1898 rows by trace_id). total 102415->100517 (-1898), remaining_corrupt=0, live stack healthy, recent ape.reflect 14/14 valid. KEY: small-batch verify caught that the raw pg_input_is_valid predicate over-counted by 213 — rerank_cross 184 + query_classify 18 + ape.reflect 11 were valid JSON behind markdown fences / think-tags that production SanitizeResponse strips. Validated all 2111 candidates through a faithful replica of llmclient.SanitizeResponse (StripThinkBlock+StripCodeFence+Trim); spared the 213 recoverable, deleted only the 1898 unparseable-after-sanitize. AUDIT PITFALL: a corrupt-data prune predicate MUST mirror the production sanitizer, not raw JSON validity. Category B (21135 error rows) + C (rerank archive/valid_golden/stale baselines) deferred this round."
"bc4np1kal8ag4tgaolatrkka", "rebase-dev-after-admin-merge", "must", "After merging a PR to main via --admin, if the dev branch has more work to push, rebase the dev branch onto main (git pu", "After merging a PR to main via --admin, if the dev branch has more work to push, rebase the dev branch onto main (git pull --rebase origin main) BEFORE pushing the next commit. This keeps the branch linear and avoids merge commits that force squash-merging. In PR #172, the GPG fix was admin-merged to main via PR #171, then the docs commit was pushed to reh3376_dev01 without rebasing — git created a merge commit, resulting in 4 commits (3 real + 1 merge) that required squash to keep history clean."
"w00hrcdsjfpwzvciby4aqmjs", "rename-before-finetune", "must_not", "Base teacher model mlx-community/Qwen3", "Base teacher model mlx-community/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-mxfp4 (Sprint C config.json SHA cdc167566e54ebe6d5c6df308649670b5f1cacfe71a198688edba8471ea64734) is read-only. Fine-tuned variants MUST use namespace mdemg/qwen3.6-35b-a3b-mdemg-v{N} (N=1,2,...). Never overwrite or re-use the base model name. User directive 2026-04-22: change the model name once we start fine-tuning so there is NO confusion. Sprint E onward enforces this."
"h9c0gruub80rtn9o82udhd97", "timestamp-format-normalization", "must", "Implemented timestamp_format enum validation: 4 formats (rfc3339, unix, unix_ms, date_only) normalized to RFC3339 on ing", "Implemented timestamp_format enum validation: 4 formats (rfc3339, unix, unix_ms, date_only) normalized to RFC3339 on ingest. New files: internal/models/timestamp.go, timestamp_test.go. Modified: models.go (TimestampFormat field on IngestRequest + BatchIngestItem), handlers.go (normalization in handleIngest + handleBatchIngest), ingest.uats.json (3 new variants). Also fixed distribution endpoint inconsistent response shape (always return stats+history wrapper). UATS: 158/158 (100%)."
"iy0t8cbin69620sn30po8k5m", "trace-all-breaks", "must_not", "FEEDBACK: When troubleshooting, never stop at the first break found", "FEEDBACK: When troubleshooting, never stop at the first break found. Trace the ENTIRE pipeline end-to-end and document ALL breaks before proposing a fix. This prevents recurring pseudo-fixes that only address one break while leaving others intact. The J17 protocol issue is a case study: multiple previous fixes each addressed one break but the system remained broken because other breaks existed downstream."
"xbegkamy8lcaee0givcowkpg", "trust-signal-must-be-persisted-never-ignore-honest", "must", "J17 trust score 25", "J17 trust score 25.4% (and Jiminy actionable compliance ~14% steady state) are NOT harmless-by-design. Operator (2026-08-01): trust reflects the receiving agents confidence in MDEMG guidance; 25.4% means the agent has learned to distrust because most surfaced items are not worth acting on. Reframe: the ~14% honest steady state and the 25.4% trust EMA are the same substrate-quality signal seen from producer + receiver sides. Do not normalize either as acceptable. The JIMINY-CORPUS + HITL-CURATION + Lever-C-tuning arc must actually raise follow rate + trust, not just make the dashboards render the low number in green."
"u45j4blh5mzu5dvv88uapucz", "unit-integration-e2e-docs", "must", "[must] All development plans MUST include three testing tiers: unit tests, integration tests, AND e2e/live tests", "[must] All development plans MUST include three testing tiers: unit tests, integration tests, AND e2e/live tests. Unit tests alone are insufficient — integration tests verify wiring between components, and e2e tests verify real behavior against running services. The neural sidecar metrics bug (latency=0, errors=0 when sidecar unreachable) was only caught by live testing, not unit tests. Plans must also include updating all relevant documentation as an explicit step. These are not optional extras — they are mandatory plan requirements."
"jnv3zpp4rog0t5g37r1mldzk", "use-cuidv2-by-default", "must", "[must] Always use CUIDv2 for identifiers", "[must] Always use CUIDv2 for identifiers"
"rktgw4xwpyn6b84kdjsto6q4", "uuid-precedent-divergence", "must", "Precedent-driven divergence incident (2026-03-23): UUID v4 was used for guidance_id and eval_id despite project-scoped C", "Precedent-driven divergence incident (2026-03-23): UUID v4 was used for guidance_id and eval_id despite project-scoped CUIDv2 requirement. Root cause chain: (1) daemon .env bug silently disabled Jiminy, so CUIDv2 constraint could not fire. (2) Existing code used uuid.New() as precedent. (3) New code copied the UUID pattern by imitation. (4) Even after Jiminy was fixed, UUID persisted because developers referenced existing code as template. Lesson: when a constraint enforcement system is down, bad patterns harden into the codebase via precedent and become self-reinforcing. Fix required touching 11 files."
